    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_one_antipodal_barycentric_support_polynomial_compiler",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 one-antipodal barycentric support has a single polynomial compiler",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a complete canonical one-antipodal candidate, one explicit even polynomial J of degree at most 5H-11, built only from E,B,C, computes the barycentric negation coloring pointwise on mu_N. Minimum support 3H+1 is equivalent to J dividing (z^N-1)/(z^2-1), having full degree, and avoiding +/-1. This removes root-cell enumeration but does not exclude the split-divisor gate.",
